 "name": "Road Green Space Scenic Beauty (SBE) in Yangling",
 "description": "Faithful replication of the aesthetic evaluation in Si, Mu & Han (2024), \"Road Landscape Design: Harmonious Relationship Between Ecology and Aesthetics\", Forests 15:2008. Participants see the paper's 13 photographs of road green space sample points in Yangling, Shaanxi, China (grass, shrub, tree and mixed plantings in traffic separation zones, roadside greenbelts and avenue greenbelts), one at a time in random order, and rate each with the Scenic Beauty Estimation scale (1 very dislike, 2 not too much, 3 average, 4 more like, 5 like). Landscape professionals also score the eight landscape character indicators of the paper's Table 1 (floristics, configuration structure, canopy density, growing status, leaf characteristic, vertical greening effect, spatial characterization, environmental harmonization; 1–5 with the paper's level labels). Original sample: 201 public questionnaires and 40 professionals. Analysis as in the paper: z-standardise each participant's SBE scores and average per sample point; combine with the standardised character score into the Scenic Beauty Index (SBI = 0.5 × SBE + 0.5 × character). Stimuli: the authors' own photographs from Figure 5 (CC BY 4.0), credited on the page; the template is removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) public and professional parts are combined into one survey with a group question that decides whether the eight indicators are shown; (2) the paper gives no wording for the questionnaire instructions or demographics, so the page adds a short introduction and asks no demographics; (3) images are cropped from the published figure at about 650 px wide; (4) the paper's ecological measurements (carbon sequestration, cooling) are not part of the survey.",
